STATES (the construction's own terms; every term below is already in the promoted amendment or the fold-effect spec)
  SNAPSHOT            := qₙ, the committed field returned across RETURN. A step CANNOT observe current-tick results;
                         re-entry is across the commit only (SPEC_J17_WORLD_FOLD_EFFECT_001 :103).
  SNAPSHOT_EFFECT_SET := E(qₙ), the distinct strict effects enabled at qₙ, computed from qₙ alone. An effect is enabled iff
                         some offered assignment U→b has ∅ ≠ ∂D ⊆ W(qₙ). Offers with the same effect (aliases, e.g. a site
                         and a face) are ONE effect; no offer is selected.
  JOINT_APPLICATION   := E(qₙ) applied together: concurrent effects jointly (disjoint changed flags and affected overlaps;
                         neither changes the other's receipt); an absorbed effect within the effect that absorbs it.
                         Conflicting effects do not occur in the amendment's scope (whole-site fields, fixed-incidence strict
                         evolution, the bound (1,0), (2,0), (4,0) carriers and offered families).
  LINK                := the commit of JOINT_APPLICATION(E(qₙ)) as qₙ₊₁, with ONE receipt computed directly:
                         discharged = W(qₙ) \ W(qₙ₊₁), opened = ∅. Per-effect receipts are NOT summed. Effects enabled by
                         qₙ₊₁ belong to the next PROPOSE.

